{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477846-dual-fellowships-for-dark-ages-mages","id":1477846,"title":"Dual Fellowships for Dark Ages mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-01T06:29:49-07:00","id":1477846,"title":"Dual Fellowships for Dark Ages mages","content":"Recent discussion on another topic got me thinking about the issue of Dark Ages mages having multiple Fellowships. Da:M rulebook and the Grimoire sourcebook allow it and provide Xp costs for additional Foundations and Pillars. M20 has an equivalent rule through the Dual Affiliation Merit, even if its very flexible Foci rules make it unnecessary in many case, except for flavor purposes and/or the benefit of having a second Affinity Sphere. This character development opportunity seems interesting, both in terms of the synergy benefits between the Foundations and Pillars of multiple Fellowships and the ability to bridge the paradigm and ideology differences between different groups. I wonder which the most fruitful Fellowship combinations would be in terms of practical benefits for magic use, likelihood of occurrence, and/or paradigm/ideological compatibility. I can think of a few good combos myself:<br /> <br /> OoH/Old Faith. One of my most preferred options, quite feasible for Hermetics that lean towards paganism or OF that have a scholarly bent, and with good synergy benefits. If you apply the setting hack of House Diedne surviving the Schism War and House Tremere being destroyed in its place, this may canon for an established subgroup, depending on whether the Diedne studied both sets of Foundation and Pillars or developed a synthesis.<br /> <br /> OoH/Messianic Voices. Not my cup of tea due to my dislike of CC/MV paradigm and ideology, but I acknowledge it is a great combo with good synergy and easy to set up.<br /> <br /> OoH/AiB. Not my cup of tea due to my dislike of the Batini way of doing things (magic should be flashy, dammit), but I acknowledge it is a great combo with good synergy and easy to set up.<br /> <br /> AiB/(non-Christian) MV. As above.<br /> <br /> Old Faith/Spirit Talkers. Good synergy, easy to justify in paradigm/ideology and organization terms.<br /> <br /> Old Faith/Valdaermen. Practically a prelude to future partial merger of the two groups in the Verbena. Just needs a paradigm/ideology balance between the zest for life of the OF and the grimness of the Val.<br /> <br /> Valdaermen/ST. Basically merging the two main mystic traditions of Norse culture into one.<br /> <br /> OoH/ST. Feasible if you got an Hermetic with a strong bent towards animism or a ST with a solid scholarly side.<br /> <br /> OoH/Valdaermen. Pursue power and suffer for it.<br /> <br /> Old Faith/(non-Abrahamic) MV. Feasible if you got a rather heterodox approach to religion.<br /> <br /> Valdaermen/(non-Abrahamic) MV. As above.<br /> <br /> Opinions? Suggestions?<br /> <br /> Yes, I know that getting adequate proficiency in two sets of Foundation and Pillars is going to take some serious effort and a sizable Xp bill, but obviously we are talking about an advanced character option here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-08-2022, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T14:15:31-07:00","id":1477866,"title":"","content":"One of the big advantage I think you're overlooking: group casting. That's the big reason to establish a metaphysical stance that embraces two Fellowships/Traditions/etc. While DAM doesn't play this up much, in M20 you can get +5 dice <b>and </b>+5 successes per roll with enough teamwork (though by the rules that's only for ritual magic, but it also takes over 100 people to get that kind of bonus). This should also be one of the big advantages for the more religious Fellowships: religions offer a ready source of a large number of believers that will gather in one place to perform rituals you can use to further boost your magic. Esp. in the DA, purposeful and deliberate applications of being flashy (also easier as a group) only helps reinforce religious communities.<br /> <br /> This also helps some of the combos above. It's important to remember that the idea of religions being &quot;exclusive&quot; is somewhat recent (and even more so in the DA setting). The idea that you would have more than one &quot;religion&quot; was actually pretty normal for a long time (still is in some places). The Romans were huge proponents of syncretism, and Christianity adopted a lot of that thinking in Europe. The whole reason why the PC Fellowships tend to be more standoffish is because they're the precursors to the Traditions; the mages that felt balancing Christian faith magic and Hermetic philosophy was completely logical and normal were the founders of the Order of Reason and that mentality helped shaped the much more internally cooperative Union (another point on the power of mages working as a group).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T03:08:25-07:00","id":1477890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477846-dual-fellowships-for-dark-ages-mages?p=1477866#post1477866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big advantage I think you're overlooking: group casting. That's the big reason to establish a metaphysical stance that embraces two Fellowships/Traditions/etc. While DAM doesn't play this up much, in M20 you can get +5 dice <b>and </b>+5 successes per roll with enough teamwork (though by the rules that's only for ritual magic, but it also takes over 100 people to get that kind of bonus). This should also be one of the big advantages for the more religious Fellowships: religions offer a ready source of a large number of believers that will gather in one place to perform rituals you can use to further boost your magic. Esp. in the DA, purposeful and deliberate applications of being flashy (also easier as a group) only helps reinforce religious communities.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true. Although as you point DA:M does not do much in terms providing rules for group casting, M20 rules on the matter seem easy to transplant. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This also helps some of the combos above. It's important to remember that the idea of religions being &quot;exclusive&quot; is somewhat recent (and even more so in the DA setting). The idea that you would have more than one &quot;religion&quot; was actually pretty normal for a long time (still is in some places). The Romans were huge proponents of syncretism, and Christianity adopted a lot of that thinking in Europe. The whole reason why the PC Fellowships tend to be more standoffish is because they're the precursors to the Traditions; the mages that felt balancing Christian faith magic and Hermetic philosophy was completely logical and normal were the founders of the Order of Reason and that mentality helped shaped the much more internally cooperative Union (another point on the power of mages working as a group). </div> </div> </div>True as well. Working from the perspective of the setting hack where the Tremere are crushed soon after turning to vampirism and the Craftmasons are destroyed at Mistridge, I suppose the Order of Reason being strangled at birth should leave the PC Fellowships more open-minded about a syncretic approach to magic. Not all mages that liked mixing Christian faith magic and Hermetic philosophy should have yet gone to the OoR side, or the 1210 Craftmasons have been enough of a bad example to taint the idea. Moreover, if House Diedne survives, their whole shtick was to be a bridge between the OoH and the OF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T13:39:50-07:00","id":1478091,"title":"","content":"I've been toying around with idea of having not Dual Foundations perhaps but learning the pillars of other Fellowships. I see it as trying to build a house with a solid foundation but with pillars of very different materials and sizes. It will work but the house will look really wonky and crooked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T19:33:39-07:00","id":1478110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477846-dual-fellowships-for-dark-ages-mages#post1477846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OoH/ST. Feasible if you got an Hermetic with a strong bent towards animism or a ST with a solid scholarly side.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those are essentially one of the larger factions within Ex Miscellanea in Ars Magica IIRC. Not really sure how you would work it out rules-wise though. \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> <br /> There was also a &quot;witches&quot; faction in Ex Misc, which could do the Old Faith blend if you wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 04-05-2022, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T07:02:57-07:00","id":1478135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477846-dual-fellowships-for-dark-ages-mages?p=1478110#post1478110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are essentially one of the larger factions within Ex Miscellanea in Ars Magica IIRC. Not really sure how you would work it out rules-wise though. \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> <br /> There was also a &quot;witches&quot; faction in Ex Misc, which could do the Old Faith blend if you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, and House Merinita in all likelihood is leaning to the witchy side as well. Just like the Ex Misc, they were one of the main House to take in the remnants of Diedne. No matter what the other subgroups and setting hacks, however, I really fancy the idea of letting the Schism War go the other way, be it by alternate timeline or time-travel intervention, and the power-hungry Tremere be crushed early instead of the framed Diedne. I never liked that part of ArM, VtM, and MtA canon, even if I acknowledge it was useful to give a spellcasting Clan and Discipline to VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-06-2022, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T18:06:37-07:00","id":1478175,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that there's probably an interesting alternate setting to explore based on the idea that House Diedne is the one that become vampires and have the Tremere wiped out as a distraction from their plot. I'm not really sure what a hypothetical &quot;Clan Diedne&quot; would look like circa 1991 and the first edition of Vampire or how such a thing might impact Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T01:36:42-07:00","id":1478193,"title":"","content":"The only thing that gave any details to House Diedne that Atlas games printed said they were a group of Druids who focused on elemental magics. A &quot;Clan Diedne &quot; would likely be highly ritualistic and would tend to manifest destructive elemental forces. The best details I've read on Druids suggests the Diedne would be obsessed with status and hyper-intellectual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T11:12:35-07:00","id":1478227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477846-dual-fellowships-for-dark-ages-mages?p=1478193#post1478193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that gave any details to House Diedne that Atlas games printed said they were a group of Druids who focused on elemental magics. A &quot;Clan Diedne &quot; would likely be highly ritualistic and would tend to manifest destructive elemental forces. The best details I've read on Druids suggests the Diedne would be obsessed with status and hyper-intellectual.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mostly agreed, except for the fact ArM made House Diedne the champions of spontaneous magic, and in DA or M20 backstory they were supposed to be paradigm hybrids between the OoH and the OF/Verbena. This makes them ill-suited to have a highly ritualistic approach to magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T14:16:45-07:00","id":1478236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477846-dual-fellowships-for-dark-ages-mages?p=1478227#post1478227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mostly agreed, except for the fact ArM made House Diedne the champions of spontaneous magic, and in DA or M20 backstory they were supposed to be paradigm hybrids between the OoH and the OF/Verbena. This makes them ill-suited to have a highly ritualistic approach to magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>On magic you have a point. But House Diedne could be hyper-ritualistic in many other things. What we know of the Druids (and the word know should be taken ironically) suggests they made life into elaborate ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T15:01:24-07:00","id":1478238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477846-dual-fellowships-for-dark-ages-mages?p=1478236#post1478236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On magic you have a point. But House Diedne could be hyper-ritualistic in many other things. What we know of the Druids (and the word know should be taken ironically) suggests they made life into elaborate ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, no problem about that. In fact, having a mostly ritualized lifestyle in mundane matters and a mostly spontaneous approach to magic might highlight their mystical and ideological concept of being living bridges between the OoH and OF paradigms and organizations. A mix of Modus and Spontaneity, indeed. I wonder if before the Tremere did their thing, the Diedne studied both sets of Foundation and Pillars, or they achieved a synthesis into proto-Spheres as the Council of Nine Traditions would do a few centuries later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T21:45:18-07:00","id":1478256,"title":"","content":"The OoH is probably the ones that best fit with most of them (AiB, MV, ST, OF) although I feel given what is overall described the first two work best since IIRC the Order 'aligns' with those other two more than ST or OF in the Dark Ages motif. I think the AiB in particular offers the closest you get to 'sphere' magick at that time (and it might narratively describe a way into Sorcerer's Crusade-era magick.) <br /> <br /> That said I can see real benefits to pair OoH with OF or ST depending on what kind you're trying to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T01:43:57-07:00","id":1478265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477846-dual-fellowships-for-dark-ages-mages?p=1478256#post1478256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OoH is probably the ones that best fit with most of them (AiB, MV, ST, OF) although I feel given what is overall described the first two work best since IIRC the Order 'aligns' with those other two more than ST or OF in the Dark Ages motif.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and admittedly, even if I personally dislike the MV paradigm, there may be real benefits from the OoH-MV combo. In an informal way, pursuit of this kind of combo to some degree may have characterized a subset of practitioners across the various 'Latin' Houses, as well as Ex Misc. The latter probably involved the Sufi or Magi/Zoroastrian kind of MV rather than the Christian one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the AiB in particular offers the closest you get to 'sphere' magick at that time (and it might narratively describe a way into Sorcerer's Crusade-era magick.) </div> </div> </div>Not sure about this kind of combo being that important for the the eventual development of the Spheres system but admittedly I am rather prejudiced against the Batini approach to magic and much more sympathetic to the Taftani alternative. Both kinds of Middle Eastern mysticism probably had more than a few sympathizers within the Order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said I can see real benefits to pair OoH with OF or ST depending on what kind you're trying to accomplish. </div> </div> </div>This is so true that from the beginning of the Order, the Hermetics have been pursuing this kind of paradigm and ideology synthesis formally or informally to some degree with the practices of various 'Pagan' Houses, including Bjornaer, Diedne, Merinita, and an important subset of Ex Misc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-08-2022, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}